---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Send one request (a file, id or name, or an ad-hoc METHOD URL) and print the response

Usage: rustman send [OPTIONS] <REQUEST|METHOD> [URL]

Arguments:
  <REQUEST|METHOD>
          A request file, its id or its name; or, with URL, the method of an ad-hoc request. A lone http(s):// URL sends an ad-hoc GET

  [URL]
          The URL of an ad-hoc request (no workspace needed)

Options:
  -H, --header <K: V>
          Ad-hoc request header (repeatable): -H 'Accept: application/json'

  -d, --data <BODY>
          Ad-hoc request body, sent as is

      --json <JSON>
          Ad-hoc JSON body (sets Content-Type and Accept to application/json)

      --body-only
          Print only the response body, redacted (as received with --show-secrets)

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write the response body, byte for byte, to FILE instead of stdout

      --show-secrets
          Print secret values and credential headers as they are, on this terminal only (history and reports stay redacted)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per request, replacing settings.timeout_ms: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or a number of milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates (exchanges are flagged insecure)

      --no-history
          Do not record the exchanges in history

  -u, --update-snapshots
          Overwrite snapshots that differ from the response (not in CI mode)

      --ci
          CI mode: never write snapshots, and fail on a missing one (also on when the CI variable is true or 1)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
